ounty, CA, US"}}, {"id": 3140420, "taxon_id": 56975, "establishment_means": "native", "place": {"id": 1930, "name": "Ventura", "display_name": "Ventura County, CA, US", "admin_level": 20, "ancestor_place_ids": [97394, 1, 14, 1930]}, "list": {"id": 68005, "title": "Asteraceae of Ventura County, CA, US"}}], "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Micropus californicus</b></i> is a plant in the daisy family which is known by the common name <b>slender cottonweed</b>. Its flowerheads resemble very small cotton balls, often rounded with cottony white hairs forming the pappus of each seed. The individual plants are known more informally as <b>Q-tips</b> due to their resemblance to the cotton swabs. It is found mostly in California, and into Oregon and northern Baja California. This plant is a resident of the vernal pool...", "vision": true}}